# --- data: fetched at runtime, never committed (acquisition code ships instead) ---
data/

# --- outputs: figures and cached results ARE committed so numbers reproduce; ---
#     everything else under outputs/ is regenerable and ignored.
#     Every .json under outputs/results/ is a published number the README or the
#     notebook reads back, so the whole directory is whitelisted rather than
#     enumerated - an enumerated list silently drops each new result file, which
#     is exactly what happened to the benchmark's own arm_summary.json.
outputs/*
!outputs/figures/
!outputs/figures/**
!outputs/results/
!outputs/results/**

# --- secrets: never commit an API key or a .env ---
.env
*.key
secrets*

# --- python / env ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Interview / recruiter prep: kept locally, never published ---------------
# These are deliverables in my own workflow (DOSSIER.md is one of the five) but
# they name prospective employers, quote recruiters' briefs, and in one case
# cross-reference a confidential assignment. They stay on disk and out of git.
DOSSIER.md
interview/
